// Fortification gates and gatehouses, baked into assets/buildings/fortifications.pak by tools/gc_artbake
// (`cargo run -p gc_artbake --release -- --config assets-src/buildings/fortifications.ron --out assets/buildings/fortifications.pak`).
// Gates for the Carrion Concord and the Brood (Iron Gate, Maw Gate): four models each, the construction
// stages `#1` (foundation), `#2` (frame) and `#3` (nearly done), then the finished gate under its own
// name, exactly as in data/rosters. Gatehouses (wall level 2: Yagura Gatehouse over the Ember Gate, Gate
// of Debts over the Iron Gate, Chitin Maw over the Maw Gate) are tier upgrades of a gate and are never
// laid as foundations, so each has only `#3` (shown in the second half of the upgrade) and the finished
// model. A gatehouse keeps its gate's 1x3 footprint and base and has a flat walkway deck at exactly 2.0
// tiles on top (parapets at most 0.35 high on the long sides, both ends open for the walls' walkways).
// Every gate or gatehouse keeps its authored positions in tiles (`keep_origin`), with the origin at the
// middle of the 1x3 footprint on the ground and the door facing +z, and shares one texture set (one
// material) between its looks. Gates and gatehouses look like the Ember Gate in size. Sources and
// scripts: the project's design/buildings/ folder (docs/21-buildings.md); the Iron Gate is
// buildings/concord/iron_gate.py, the Maw Gate buildings/brood/maw_gate.py, and the gatehouses are
// buildings/ember/yagura_gatehouse.py, buildings/concord/gate_of_debts.py and buildings/brood/chitin_maw.py.
// More faction fortifications (walls, towers) join this pack later.
(
